# Peregrine VTOL tail-sitter: PX4 stage 2 - use the airspeed sensor for control
# Target firmware: PX4 v1.17.x, board holybro_kakuteh7
#
# Load this ONLY after:
#   - the Matek ASPD-4525 shows up (QGC -> MAVLink Inspector -> AIRSPEED / VFR_HUD),
#   - the differential pressure offset is calibrated (QGC -> Sensors -> Airspeed),
#   - blowing into the pitot moves the airspeed reading and it settles near 0 at rest.
# Required before any run faster than about 25 m/s: without it the forward-flight gains
# are not reduced with speed.
#
# Equivalent of ArduPilot ARSPD_USE 1.
#
# Format: Vehicle-Id <TAB> Component-Id <TAB> Name <TAB> Value <TAB> Type (6 = INT32, 9 = REAL32)
#
# use the measured airspeed for gain scaling, airspeed control and the transition logic
1	1	FW_USE_AIRSPD	1	6
# refuse to arm if the airspeed sensor is missing
1	1	SYS_HAS_NUM_ASPD	1	6
# data-missing, data-stuck and innovation checks (PX4 default)
1	1	ASPD_DO_CHECKS	7	6
# if the sensor fails in flight, fall back to the ground-speed-minus-wind estimate
1	1	ASPD_FALLBACK	1	6
